  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "9605ba6f8e834b9091677859b462a729_4",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 272 IPC makes punishable an offence by a person, who adulterates any article of food or drink."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "22b16264156f479399f290dfdb247944_5",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, this Section would only come into play if food or drink is adulterated."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c3b9f2af31b24b0692e80255ce2621fd_6",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Indian Penal Code does not describe or define adulteration."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a8493dd380f14688a479d5041b761b77_7",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The definition of adulterant is found in the provisions of the FSS Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6f48be2da4b84cf1962d4458ed84d08f_8",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "According to the said definition as found in Section 3(1)(a) of the FSS Act, adulterant is a material which could make the food unsafe or sub-standard or mis-branded."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "628ff873712a45bfaee497c40451f71b_9",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, according to Section 272 IPC, if a material is used to make the food unsafe/sub-standard or mis-branded, then only the offence would be attracted."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "81670dd2bd984ec58101085ba707c2b2_10",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the case on hand, as tobacco or tobacco products do not come within the definition of food or drink, these products do not come within the ambit of Section 272 IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c2305ac803b64d2ea31fa9145e7ec347_11",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Similarly, Section 273 IPC talks of the sale of a noxious food or drink."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "56ebb6a75e6d43d3b097bbf416538fe0_12",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If a person offers for sale a \"food or drink\" any article which has become noxious or is in a state of unfit for \"food or drink\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a74958bb8e45477e943db1ed9b57af30_13",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This section would apply, when an article which has become noxious or which has been rendered noxious."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "769da64ba9814792a1c0b10e8e9722a0_14",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It also applies to food or drink only."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f634fc28a5ab4dafbb74bdeda9534239_15",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The word noxious is not defined in IPC, but as per the dictionary meaning noxious means harmful, deleterious, injurious, poisonous etc."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bc8f6179c7e04768a29faebd40f717dd_16",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nSection 188 IPC is also being pressed into service repeatedly in these cases."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c0c7541333c148ef9ed3135d1adb40cc_17",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As per the settled law on the subject, section 188 IPC would apply to the disobedience of an Divvela Pulla Rao vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 23 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/38653079/\n1 order duly promulgated"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7b301e442e6249239f0f4f97108be222_18",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As per the settled law on the subject,\nbefore an accused is charged, there must be (1) an order duly promulgated by the public servant (2) the public servant must have the lawful authority to promulgate the order (3) the person flouting the"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1173031819f845a0ab89766f385fcd30_19",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The judgment of the Division Bench of the Allahabad High Court in Boop Singh Tyagi v. State6 is appropriate in the circumstances."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "570df84b002d454a9c5163d360a5b398_20",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The right to promulgate the ordinance/order is also an issue which is being raised, because under the FSS Act, the Commissioner of Food Safety alone has the authority to pass the orders only if the article of food can causes danger or is in"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c15abdab9e914a50b56e68192caed76e_21",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nSince the matter is supposedly before the Writ Court, this Court is not expressing any further opinion, but the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner, Sri Raja Reddy, that such a notification can only be issued for emergency"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3940ebde371c4d429c96dde70386c076_22",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This Court holds that the offence under Section 188 IPC., is also not attracted since the necessary pre-conditions are not satisfied."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "400a93b2768c4ec7b2d68213e350b343_23",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 353 IPC is also pressed into service by the police in these cases."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ceb2857135424c29a6e3eff770e3e6f0_24",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the case on hand, the only issue that is raised is that the accused pushed away the police officer while trying to escape."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "de89cb840ec34dc89db931ce475903f1_25",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This by itself, in the opinion of this Court, would not amount to use of assault or criminal force against a public servant from discharging of his duties."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9ede3409827345fabce6c1fd694d90d7_26",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 420 IPC is also being added in some of these cases."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "28fc2a62bb1d42a7b2087d1d4513a241_27",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This Court notices that the essential ingredients for utilizing the section are not at all fulfilled."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ef60b36026d04b158057d145c0157d52_28",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "There is neither inducement nor delivery of any property to bring in the ingredients of section 420 IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1d33a81db2cf42b3b4769c1150e868f5_29",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As per the settled law on the subject, this intention must be present from the inception."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "312236f7706a4ebf9d611eb302fa2149_30",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The police are in fact third parties to the offence of cheating and therefore, whether they can maintain a complaint under Section 420 IPC is also debatable."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f77ecf66e84c4a8c9d3aef70126df49f_31",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The related sections from 415 IPC are also not applicable as this Court is of the opinion that as on date, the trade in tobacco products is not barred."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4f533500a7bf4249bbdb3b2ee9856b76_32",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This Court is constrained to reiterate all these issues once again, despite the order passed by the learned single Judge in Crl.P.No.3731 of 2018 and batch."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "80f95043aed84ba4b22e5b90054715e8_33",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The conclusions of the single Judge in the said batch are fully agreed to by this Court also."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e9f665612bf5491ebc2c774679454063_34",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "None of the sections of the IPC or the FSS Act,\nwhich are pressed into service are applicable to the facts and circumstances of the case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "516d583fab37493186ef40b23ae4951d_35",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Since the notifications issued by the State Government are said to be the subject matter of different challenge in the original writ jurisdiction, this Court is not pronouncing on the same."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cedb975a4100428aac12a81b9724144f_36",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
        "explicit_leakage_phrase"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bquashed\\b",
          "matched_text": "quashed",
          "start": 453,
          "end": 460
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "\nBut as far as the present cases are concerned, this Court by exercising the power under section 482 Cr.P.C and following the mandate of the Honble Supreme Court of India in State of Haryana v.\nBhajan lal and the judgment of the High Court "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "50f021814cf9499e8cdf7bc770483f35_37",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The offences under the NDPS Act can be pursued."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4c684cfc36494861a5d41f5b6fa30ecf_38",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The offences under the COTPA Act, can only be launched if the police find that the sections 5, 6 7 and 10 are not complied with."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "247e757a9ac048e1a2a7662b14ce516b_39",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Except on these very limited grounds genuine/legitimate traders cannot be prosecuted."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "12f0f37330854ee3bac3dc1c93ff366c_40",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nIt is hoped that copies of the orders passed by the learned single Judge in Crl.P.No.3731 of 2018 and batch and this order are widely circulated by the Director General of Police and the Chief Secretary of the State of Andhra Pradesh throu"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "be45dce8967440ac8af481449d40bbe5_41",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Whatever be the impact of tobacco products on the health of an individual or the nation; till the law is amended/modified it has to be followed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4b9feaa52aa145679881941833506f76_42",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As held by many Courts earlier; it may be hard, but it is the law."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "57cb7cc4ca2e430684690eaf4e186538_43",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "With the above observations, the criminal petitions are allowed.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "568659dfca1b423f9b4e699a56633616_44",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc",
        "explicit_leakage_phrase"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bpetition\\s+is\\s+allowed\\b",
          "matched_text": "petition is allowed",
          "start": 212,
          "end": 231
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "4. Hence, following the said Orders passed by this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, dated 18.12.2019, and taking into consideration of the facts and circumstances of the case,\nthis criminal petition is allowed by quash"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b5a90e0c821f407ebc083e3dbbac5c17_45",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
